ef 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186345997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9ea9fa5e-7580-5121-9429-ea3965fd0aec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348324 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348324 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80049" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348324 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348324 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $Q(1,3,4)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-4,2,0⟩=2$, find the shortest distance from $P(5,-2,3)$ to $Π.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348324 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "799391e6-f2b4-56d4-b2e4-fcfb4ba4b2c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348324 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,3,4⟩-⟨5,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-4,2,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-4)\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 0|}{\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|16+10+0|}{\\sqrt{16+4+0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|26|}{\\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348334 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348334 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80118" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348334 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348334 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-7,5,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-8y+8z=-36.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348334 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "13132844-a558-54b3-bea9-4e5aeb81c059" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348334 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-8y+8z & =-36 \\\\ 4(-1)-8(1)+8z & =-36 \\\\ 8z & =-24 \\\\ z & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-1,1,-3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-1,1,-3⟩-⟨-7,5,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-4,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-8,8⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-8)+(-5)\\cdot 8|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{8}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|24+32-40|}{\\sqrt{16+64+64}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,16\\,|}{\\sqrt{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476200 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186476980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476200 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186476984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476200 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186476987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476200 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186476996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186